    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Understand one draft video segment and persist a reusable sidecar snapshot.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --prompt TEXT       Editing-oriented understanding prompt; defaults to people and\r\n                              visual content\r\n          --analysis-module TEXT ... \r\n                              Analysis module. Repeatable: face-identity, gender,\r\n                              visual-content\r\n          --analysis-level TEXT:{low,medium,high} \r\n                              Sampling detail level: low / medium / high\r\n          --frame-interval TEXT \r\n                              Frame sampling interval. Use an explicit duration unit:\r\n                              us/ms/s/min\r\n          --timeout TEXT      Bounded provider timeout. Use an explicit duration unit:\r\n                              us/ms/s/min; maximum 10min\r\n          --content-fingerprint TEXT \r\n                              Trusted source content fingerprint override\r\n          --expected-record-revision TEXT:NONNEGATIVE \r\n                              Expected sidecar record revision for CAS\r\n          --refresh           Ignore a matching sidecar analysis and replace it\r\n          --allow-partial-cache \r\n                              Allow an exact partial analysis snapshot to satisfy the request\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Analyze people, gender and visual content for one draft segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo material-understand --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID> \\\r\n      --analysis-module face-identity --analysis-module gender \\\r\n      --analysis-module visual-content\r\n  # Replace an existing snapshot with bounded provider execution\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo material-understand --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID> \\\r\n      --refresh --analysis-level high --timeout 5min\r\n\r\nRESULT CONTRACT\r\n  - The command writes only the Material Understanding attachment sidecar.\r\n  - Versioned subject_ref values are returned in analysis.subjects[].\r\n  - Server callers must not invent or guess VE face_id values.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
